  [
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/contentPages/1",
      "value": "With a homeworld sparse in strong metals, the dawning of warfare saw swords reach a value far beyond that of nearly any known culture (historically speaking, even including Humanity, nothing comes close). Finding enough metal with which to form long-lasting blades was expensive, and led to a strong cultural importance to swords."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/contentPages/1",
      "value": "戦剣の興隆は、金属が強く、家庭に疎いため、既知の文化(歴史的に言えば、人間性を含めても、何も近づきません)のほとんどよりもはるかに価値があります。 長持ちする刀を造るだけの金属を見つけるのに費用がかかり、刀剣の文化的重要性が強かった。"
    }
  ],
  [
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/contentPages/2",
      "value": "It was believed that a warrior and his blade were forever bound, and drew strength and power from one another (and could transfer this power back and forth, often observed in ancient rituals known as Conshak). A warrior either passed his weapon on to his child, or was buried with the weapon should no heirs remain to inherit the strength of their father. To take another's blade was a 'shameful act' practiced only by desperate cowards or outcasts."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/contentPages/2",
      "value": "戦士と彼の剣は永遠に束縛され、互いに力と力を引いていたと信じられていた(そして、しばしばコンシャクとして知られている古代の儀式で観察されるように、この力を前後に転送することができました)。 武士は自分の武器を子供に渡すか、父の強さを継承するために相続人が残っていない場合、武器で埋葬されました。 他人の刃をとることは、必死の卑劣者や暴徒によってのみ実践される「恥ずべき行為」であった。"
    }
  ],
  [
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/contentPages/3",
      "value": "Some blades would pass for hundreds (perhaps even thousands) of years from one hand to the next within a single family (or be won in duels or by war). Even today some swords can be traced back nearly five thousand years! Most of this age have long since passed the point of usefulness due to the natural process of aging or by excessive use in battle. These pieces are largely symbolic in importance, and in many cases are a mark of nobility."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/contentPages/3",
      "value": "幾つかの刃物は、一家の中で数百年(おそらく数千年)、一家の中で次々に受け継がれていく(あるいは、決闘や戦争で勝った)。 今日でも、五千年近く遡ることができる剣がいくつかあります! この年齢のほとんどは、老化の自然な過程や戦闘における過度な使用のために、長い間有用性点を通過してきました。 これらの作品は重要で、しばしば貴族の印である。"
    }
  ],
  [
